   "rule_summary": "Manufacturers must report every known thermal incident involving overheating, fire, injury, or material property damage to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, with an initial account even if facts remain incomplete. Affected customers must be notified within 72 hours when the incident presents a credible safety risk to their unit or requires customer action.",
