   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before sale and at least annually thereafter, using a documented, independently auditable protocol and representative samples. Manufacturers must provide complete per-model results, including failure rates, to the relevant regulator and directly to customers purchasing that model. Customer disclosure must be limited to those customers and must not require public posting or broad publication of individual-company per-model failure rates. A failure rate above 5% requires a regulator-approved corrective-action plan and retesting within 12 months; it does not by itself require market exclusion. Regulators may impose interim safeguards or restrict sales where evidence indicates an imminent risk."
